WF-26 — Re-Engaged Opted-Out User Handler

## Summary

- Inputs (WF-01 canonical envelope per data-contract-discipline Phase 1 — design.md §2.1, opted-out variant per TD-DCP-105): `phoneNumber` (E.164 string), `messageType` (text|interactive), `messageContent` (string), `user` (object: {id, phone_number, name, status='opted_out', slack_channel_id, current_consultation_id} — must be non-null and `status` must be `opted_out`), `pendingUser` (must be null on this branch — opted_out users have no pending row), `wasOptedOut` (boolean, must be `true`). Additionally carries the standard WF-01 passthrough fields (`rawMessage`, `messageContentUpper`, `messageId`, `timestamp`, `contactName`, `metadata`) — forwarded unchanged to WF-02 in Step 6.
- Outputs: One outbound WhatsApp text message (personalized welcome-back). User row updated to `status='consultation_closed'`. Inbound message re-entered into the state machine via WF-02 so the user's first re-engagement message is actually answered, not just acknowledged.
- State Transitions: `users.status: opted_out → consultation_closed`. No `current_consultation_id` change (left as-is; a prior session, if any, was already closed at opt-out time by WF-47).
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-50 (Send WhatsApp), WF-02 (User State Router).
- **Notes:**
  - Uniform re-entry status: every re-engagement lands at `consultation_closed` regardless of the pre-opt-out state. No `pre_opt_out_status` column; no per-prior-state branching. Q1 design decision locked 2026-05-25 in sprint `data-contract-sprint-bug-fix` handoff `handoff-td-dcp-105-done-wf26-build-pending.md`.
  - Forward-routing first message: after sending the welcome-back, WF-26 calls WF-02 with the refreshed envelope (`user.status='consultation_closed'`) so the user's first re-engagement message routes through the state machine in one turn rather than requiring a follow-up. Q2 design decision (locked, same source).
  - Welcome wording is unified across pre-opt-out states (no special variant for users who opted out from `payment_submitted`). Q4 design decision (locked, same source).
  - The `Refresh Envelope Status` Set v3.4 node (Step 3) MUST set `includeOtherFields: true` and overwrite `user.status` to `consultation_closed` on the in-flight envelope. Without this refresh, WF-02 sees the pre-UPDATE `opted_out` status and routes incorrectly (cf. Set v3.4 default-drop foot-gun, plugin Step 5f.5).
  - Entry guard at Step 1 follows the WF-02 pattern — defense-in-depth per design.md §2.1 + §2.7. WF-26 is in design.md §3.3 entry-guard scope per the 2026-05-25 Amendment (sprint `data-contract-sprint-bug-fix`): post-TD-DCP-107 WF-26 became a direct WF-01 downstream on the opted-out re-engagement branch, parallel to WF-02's role on the main path. The guard throws loudly on contract violation (envelope shape, non-null `pendingUser`, `wasOptedOut !== true`, `user.status !== 'opted_out'`).

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Validate Inputs (entry guard — defense-in-depth per design.md §2.1 + §2.7). Read envelope from the workflow trigger. Throw with descriptive error if:
  - phoneNumber is missing or not a string.
  - messageType is not one of: text, interactive.
  - messageContent key is absent or null.
  - user is null/undefined OR user.id is missing OR user.status !== 'opted_out'.
  - pendingUser is non-null (contract violation — opted_out users have no pending row).
  - wasOptedOut !== true.
  Pass through unchanged on success.

Step 2: UPDATE chinmay_astro.users SET status = 'consultation_closed', updated_at = NOW() WHERE id = user.id RETURNING id, phone_number, name, status, slack_channel_id, current_consultation_id. Single-row update; if affected rows = 0 the workflow halts (contract failure — user.id should exist by construction since the envelope carries the loaded row).

Step 3: Refresh the in-flight envelope's `user.status` to `consultation_closed` (overwrite the stale `opted_out` value) so the WF-02 call in Step 6 routes on the post-UPDATE state. Pass through every other envelope field unchanged. (Set v3.4 with `includeOtherFields: true`.)

Step 4: Build the welcome-back WF-50 payload (canonical §2.3 contract): `{phoneNumber, messageType: 'text', messageContent: "Welcome back, ${user.name}. Since you'd opted out, your previous session has ended. This is a fresh start. You don't need to send birth details again — we have them on file."}`. Personalization uses `user.name` from the envelope.

Step 5: Call WF-50 (Send WhatsApp) with the welcome-back payload from Step 4. Fire-and-forget from WF-26's perspective — WF-50 owns its own logging via WF-60.

Step 6: Call WF-02 (User State Router) with the refreshed envelope from Step 3 (passthrough mode — the envelope already matches §2.1 shape with the updated `user.status`). WF-02 then routes the inbound message based on `messageType` + the refreshed `user.status='consultation_closed'` — which means a button_reply lands in WF-43 / WF-44 / WF-45 logic, plain text lands in WF-43's intent classifier path, etc. The user's first re-engagement message is answered in the same turn.

Step 7: End.
